   "name": "Uniform Enduring Powers of Attorney Act",
   "year": 2015,
   "amended": 2021,
   "body": "Uniform Law Conference of Canada",
   "sourceUrl": "https://ulcc-chlc.ca/ULCC/media/EN-Uniform-Acts/Consolidated-Uniform-Enduring-Powers-of-Attorney-Act-(2015)-as-Amended-2021.pdf",
   "summary": "Model EPOA takes effect on the latest of signing, a stated date or a stated triggering event (s 11(1)). If it springs on incapacity, a qualified health care provider may confirm incapacity (s 11(2)). Authority ends on a specified date, written revocation, the grantor's death, the attorney's death, incapacity or resignation, appointment of a guardianship decision-maker, and spousal separation (s 17). The 2021 amendments added electronic EPOAs. The year is 2015 (amended 2021), not 2008.",
